{title: 015 - My Maker and My King}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #015 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 15}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]My Maker [F/C]and [C]my King, To [G]Thee [C/G]my [G7]all I [C]owe;
[C]Thy sovereign [F/C]bounty [C]is the [G]spring [Am/C]Whence [G/D]all my blessings flow;
[G]Thy [C]sovereign bounty is the spring [F]Whence [Dm]all [G7]my [C/G]blessings flow;
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]The creature of Thy [G7]hand,
[C]On Thee alone I [G7]live;
[C]My God, [F/C]Thy [C]benefits [G/D]demand
[C]More praise than [G]I can give.
[G]My [C]God, Thy benefits [G7]demand
[G]More [C]praise than I [Dm]can [C/G]give.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Lord, what can I impart
[C]When all is Thine before?
[C]Thy love [F/C]demands [G]a [Am/C]thankful [Dm]heart;
[C]The gift, alas! [G/D]how poor.
[G]Thy [C]love demands a [F]thankful [G]heart;
[G]The [C]gift, alas! [Dm]how [C/G]poor.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]O! let Thy grace inspire
[C]My soul with strength divine;
[C]Let every [G]word [Am/C]each [G/D]desire
[C]And all my [G]days be Thine.
[G]Let [C]every word [F]each [G7]desire
[G]And [C]all my days [Dm]be [C/G]Thine.
{end_of_verse}
